From: Orion <orionopenwow@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] openvanilla: never drop the body through an unloaded world on login

The post-snap settle hold (login, teleport, summon) freezes the body with gravity off until the
tile under it is presentable. Its stall backstop turned gravity back on after 6 s without stream
progress, whether or not the tile under the body had ground yet. On a slow first load (cold
cache, a busy CDN, a weak machine) the body then fell through the world on login.

Now a stall gives up only over ground: the body's own tile resident with its colliders attached.
Without ground the hold keeps the body still, under the loading cover, up to SETTLE_HARD_CAP
(45 s), so a truly dead stream still lets go. The server side (mangos patch 0018) rescues anyone
who falls anyway.
(player.rs re-exports SETTLE_HARD_CAP next to SETTLE_TIMEOUT, so world_focus.rs can use it.)

diff --git a/crates/benilla-app/src/player.rs b/crates/benilla-app/src/player.rs
